# VitalPet — Feature Domain Logic Conventions

## Core principle
Every file in `lib/features/<feature>/domain/` and `lib/core/` is pure Dart — zero Flutter framework dependencies. These are testable with `dart test` in isolation, no widget tree required.

## Feature layer boundaries
| Layer | Owns | Must NOT |
|---|---|---|
| `domain/` | Pure Dart logic, Riverpod notifiers, use-case functions | Import `package:flutter/*`, touch the DB directly |
| `data/` | Drift DAOs, the drift-generated code | Contain business logic |
| `presentation/` | Screens, widgets, Rive integration | Contain business logic |
| `lib/core/` | DB setup, encryption, audit, constants | Contain feature-specific logic |

## ModeSelector — pure function
```dart
// lib/features/check_in/domain/mode_selector.dart
enum CheckInMode { quick, guided, companion }

/// Pure function — no side effects, no dependencies.
/// Score [1,3] → companion (Mode 3)
/// Score [4,6] → guided (Mode 2)
/// Score [7,10] → quick (Mode 1)
CheckInMode selectMode(int wellnessScore) {
  if (wellnessScore <= 3) return CheckInMode.companion;
  if (wellnessScore <= 6) return CheckInMode.guided;
  return CheckInMode.quick;
}
```

## VitalityCalculator — pure function
```dart
// lib/features/pet/domain/vitality_calculator.dart
/// Graduated missed-day penalty: day 1 = -8, day 2 = -10, day 3+ = -12 each.
/// Base = 60, streak bonus up to +30, depth bonus 0–10.
/// If [isVulnerabilityFrozen] is true, no penalty is applied.
int calculateVitality({
  required int streak,
  required double checkInDepthScore, // 0.0–1.0
  required List<int> consecutiveMissedDays,
  required bool isVulnerabilityFrozen,
}) {
  const base = 60;
  final streakBonus = streak.clamp(0, 30);
  final depthBonus = (checkInDepthScore * 10).round();

  var penalty = 0;
  if (!isVulnerabilityFrozen) {
    for (var i = 0; i < consecutiveMissedDays.length; i++) {
      penalty += switch (i) { 0 => 8, 1 => 10, _ => 12 };
    }
  }

  return (base + streakBonus + depthBonus - penalty).clamp(0, 100);
}
```
**Never store intermediate vitality — always recompute from raw check-in log (NFR-R-03).**

## SLM client pattern
```dart
// lib/features/slm/slm_client.dart
// Uses flutter_gemma. Enforces 3-second timeout.
// Returns SLMOutput on success, throws SLMTimeoutException on timeout.

class SLMClient {
  static const _timeoutMs = 3000;

  Future<SLMOutput> generateQuestions(SLMContext context) async {
    final promptJson = context.toPromptJson();
    try {
      final raw = await FlutterGemma.instance
          .getResponseAsync(promptJson)
          .timeout(const Duration(milliseconds: _timeoutMs));
      return _parseAndValidate(raw);
    } on TimeoutException {
      throw SLMTimeoutException();
    }
  }
}
// Caller catches SLMTimeoutException and calls RuleBasedFallback.getQuestions(context)
```

## MedicalContentFilter — mandatory wrapper
```dart
// lib/features/slm/medical_content_filter.dart
class FilterResult {
  final bool safe;
  final String text; // use this — never the raw SLM output
  const FilterResult({required this.safe, required this.text});
}

// EVERY SLM-generated string shown to the user must go through this:
final result = MedicalContentFilter.filter(rawSlmOutput);
if (!result.safe) {
  await AuditLogDao.append(AuditEvent.filterTrigger(
    payloadHash: _hash(rawSlmOutput),
  ));
}
// Use result.text — never rawSlmOutput
```
Patterns loaded from `config/medical_filter_patterns.json` at app startup. Do not hardcode patterns.

## Drift repositories — naming conventions
```dart
// All DB access through DAOs in lib/features/<feature>/data/ or lib/core/
// DO use the DAO:
final checkins = await ref.read(checkInDaoProvider).findByDateRange(start, end);

// DON'T write raw SQL in domain or presentation:
// final result = await db.customSelect('SELECT ...')  ← WRONG
```

## AuditLogDao — append only
```dart
// lib/core/audit/audit_log_dao.dart
// append() is the ONLY method — no update, no delete, no clear
Future<void> append(AuditEvent event) { ... }
Future<void> appendInTransaction(Transaction tx, AuditEvent event) { ... }
```

## Riverpod provider patterns
```dart
// Domain notifiers use AsyncNotifier for async state:
@riverpod
class CheckInSession extends _$CheckInSession {
  @override
  Future<CheckInSessionState> build() async => CheckInSessionState.idle();

  Future<void> submitWellnessScore(int score) async { ... }
  Future<void> submitAnswer(QuestionAnswer answer) async { ... }
  Future<void> completeSession() async { ... }
}

// Pure computed providers use Provider or FutureProvider:
@riverpod
CheckInMode currentMode(CurrentModeRef ref) {
  final score = ref.watch(wellnessScoreProvider);
  return score != null ? selectMode(score) : CheckInMode.quick;
}
```

## Testing requirements
Domain logic must have unit tests. Minimum coverage:
- `VitalityCalculator`: all boundary values, consecutive missed days escalation, vulnerability freeze
- `ModeSelector`: score 3, 4, 6, 7 boundary values
- `MedicalContentFilter`: known blocked phrases return safe=false; safe content passes through
- `BaselineTracker`: deviation detection with 14-day time series fixtures

Run before committing: `flutter test test/features/<feature>/`

## Code generation
drift and Riverpod use code generation. After modifying any annotated file:
```bash
dart run build_runner build --delete-conflicting-outputs
```
Never edit `.g.dart` or `.freezed.dart` files manually — they are regenerated.
